---
import ScienceFront from '../components/ScienceFront.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { articles } from '../lib/content';
const stories=(await articles()).filter(a=>/climate|wildlife|environment|conservation|biodiversity/i.test(a.category?.title||'') || /\b(climate|wildlife|biodiversity|drought|heatwave|coral reefs?|endangered species|mangroves)\b/i.test(a.title)).sort((a,b)=>Date.parse(b.publishedAt)-Date.parse(a.publishedAt));
---
<Layout title="Climate Change & Wildlife | ATHENA" description="Reporting on a changing climate, wildlife and the communities that depend on thriving ecosystems.">
<div class="desk"><ScienceFront title="Climate & Wildlife" stories={stories} links={[['Documentary Room','documentaries','Watch the natural world'],['Field studies','studies','Explore the research'],['Science reading','reading','Earth observation and analysis'],['Newsroom','reporting','Read ATHENA’s coverage']]} /><h2 id="documentaries">Documentary room</h2><div class="grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">NETFLIX · ARCHIVE DOCUMENTARY</p><h3>Our Planet: Coastal Seas</h3><iframe title="Our Planet: Coastal Seas" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/r9PeYPHdpNo" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen></iframe><p>Follow sharks and sea urchins through the shallow waters where reefs, kelp and other coastal habitats shelter marine life.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r9PeYPHdpNo">Watch Coastal Seas on Netflix’s YouTube channel →</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">NETFLIX · ARCHIVE DOCUMENTARY</p><h3>Our Planet: Forests</h3><iframe title="Our Planet: Forests" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/JkaxUblCGz0" loading="lazy" allowfullscreen></iframe><p>From eagles to Siberian tigers, this episode follows animals whose survival depends on the forest around them.</p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JkaxUblCGz0">Watch Forests on Netflix’s YouTube channel →</a></article></div>
<h2 id="studies">Studies worth reading</h2><div class="grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">FIELD STUDY · TANZANIA · 2008</p><h3>Which elephant calves survived a severe drought?</h3><p>Researchers followed elephant families in Tarangire during the 1993–94 drought. Their records let readers compare calf survival across families in the same ecosystem, without assuming every herd responded alike.</p><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2610102/">Read the elephant study →</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">REEF SURVEYS · AUSTRALIA · 2017</p><h3>Why did some stretches of reef bleach more severely?</h3><p>Scientists compared aerial and underwater observations with sea temperatures across three Great Barrier Reef bleaching events. The hardest-hit areas shifted with the location of the heat; local protection offered little defence against the extreme temperatures of 2016.</p><a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/nature21707">Read the study in Nature →</a></article></div>
<h2 id="reading">From other science desks</h2><article><p class="eyebrow">NASA EARTH OBSERVATORY · 13 NOVEMBER 2026</p><h3>A Global Rebound for Mangroves</h3><p>Look closely at the same stretch of Myanmar’s coastline in 2010 and 2026. Side-by-side Landsat images reveal where mangroves expanded, giving readers a way to see a changing habitat for themselves.</p><a href="https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/a-global-rebound-for-mangroves/">Read NASA’s illustrated article →</a></article><h2>Explore the beat</h2><div class="grid"><article><h3>Climate &amp; communities</h3><p>How heat, rainfall and changing seasons affect water, livelihoods, schools and health.</p></article><article><h3>Wildlife &amp; habitats</h3><p>Species, the landscapes they depend on, and the people working to protect both.</p></article></div></div>
</Layout>
<style>.desk{max-width:1080px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1.5rem;border-top:5px solid #a91935}.desk h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,6vw,4.6rem);line-height:1.08}.desk h2{margin-top:2.5rem}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,260px),1fr));gap:1.2rem}.grid article{border-top:1px solid #aaa;padding:1rem 0}.grid a{color:inherit}.desk p{line-height:1.55}.desk iframe{width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;border:0}.desk nav{line-height:2}.desk nav a{color:#89162d}</style>
